  "title": "Iqa‘ Fox 2/4",
  "subtitle": "Examples of the slower form of Iqa‘ Fox that can be notated in 4/4",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Fox",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Fox (probably derived from \"Foxtrot\") is a simple 2/4 iqa‘ that is usually played without too much ornamentation over instrumental sections. This, and the fact it is often played at very fast tempos, gives it a swift and urgent feel. It is the main iqa‘ used in the Turkish/Eastern European Longa Ottoman instrumental form. Fox can readily modulate to Malfuf and back. A very slow version of Fox (see the last 2 examples) could be notated as 4/4."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Fox 2/4 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Fox Iqa‘ Fox (probably derived from \"Foxtrot\") is a simple 2/4 iqa‘ that is usually played without too much ornamentation over instrumental sections. This, and the fact it is often played at very fast tempos, gives it a swift and urgent feel. It is the main iqa‘ used in the Turkish/Eastern European Longa Ottoman instrumental form. Fox can readily modulate to Malfuf and back. A very slow version of Fox (see the last 2 examples) could be notated as 4/4. Longa Farahfaza (Instrumental) Salim Sahhab Orchestra Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Ghulubt Asalih Fi Ruhi (1946) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Al-Fann (1945) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Tuta (1942) Instrumental Composition (from the movie Ahlam el-Shabab ) Music by Farid al-Atrash Examples of the slower form of Iqa‘ Fox that can be notated in 4/4 Ya Dunya Ya Gharami (1938) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Kulli Da Kan Leh (1954) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Iqa‘ Fox 2/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
